# ============================================================================
# benchmarks/ — per-language generated build artifacts
# ============================================================================
#
# Committed:   input.kz, Program.cs/*.csproj, main.rs/Cargo.toml/Cargo.lock,
#              bench.py, bench.js, README.md files, scripts/, results/*.csv
# Generated:   everything below, plus what's already in the root .gitignore.
#
# Already covered globally by /.gitignore — do NOT repeat here:
#   .zig-cache/, zig-out/, a.out, *_emitted.zig, node_modules/
#
# Patterns below add the per-language artifacts that the global rules miss.

# Koru emitted files (workloads/<wl>/koru/) — same shape as the
# tests/regression/**/<file> rules in the root .gitignore.
**/koru/backend.zig
**/koru/backend.err
**/koru/backend.out
**/koru/build.zig
**/koru/build.zig.zon
**/koru/build_backend.zig
**/koru/build_output.zig
**/koru/compile_*.err
**/koru/compiler_env.zig
**/koru/program_ast.zig

# C# build outputs (workloads/<wl>/csharp/)
**/csharp/bin/
**/csharp/obj/
**/csharp/out/

# Rust build output (workloads/<wl>/rust/)
# Cargo.lock is intentionally committed for reproducible benchmark builds.
**/rust/target/

# Python bytecode cache (workloads/<wl>/python/)
**/python/__pycache__/
**/python/*.pyc
